<article class="env-corollary" id="05FG">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05FG">Corollary <span data-tag="05FG">4.7.2.8</span> <span class="named">(Homotopy Invariance)</span>.</a> Let $F: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ be an equivalence of $\infty $-categories and let $f: X \rightarrow Y$ be a morphism of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$. Then $f$ is $n$-truncated if and only if the image $F(f): F(X) \rightarrow F(Y)$ is $n$-truncated. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Using Corollary <a data-tag="02GL" href="/tag/02GL">4.6.4.21</a>, we see that $F$ induces an equivalence of $\infty $-categories $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{/Y} \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}_{ / F(Y) }$. The desired result now follows by combining Proposition <a data-tag="05FF" href="/tag/05FF">4.7.2.7</a> with Remark <a data-tag="05EJ" href="/tag/05EJ">4.7.1.14</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</article>
